Sim Thiam Chye wrote:
> I tried to re-direct syslogd output from a OSF3.2G m/c to a OSF4.0D m/c
> without success.

At V4.0D you need a file /etc/syslog.auth containing the names of the
machines to accept syslog messages from. Sadly this did not make it into the
man page yet, you need to look it up in the release notes.

You may also need a patch to syslogd: the original 4.0D release contained a
bug where syslogd would die at startup, depending on the exact size of the
syslog.auth file. If your syslogd stays alive then you do not need the patch.

