Paul Dwerryhouse (paul@xenu.ee.mu.oz.au) wrote:
: 
: Here's a fun one:
: 
: I just updated the firmware on an Alpha 200 4/233 to V6.6, and now the 
: video won't synchronise on the console. The display just continually rolls 
: and stretches the text right across the screen (both when it's in text mode
: and when it kicks X) so that it is totally unreadable.
: 
: I rebooted it with a dumb terminal attached, and brought the firmware version
: back to V6.5, but I'm still getting the same problem.
: 
: The graphics card was working fine before I did this - Does anyone have
: any idea how I can fix this?

There is a console environment variable "tga_sync_green".  The value of this
variable is a number 0-7.  The number is actually a bit-map, with:

        1 = video card 0 has sync on green
        2 = video card 1 has sync on green
        3 = video cards 0 and 1 have sync on green
        
and so on.

In prior versions, you could just the variable to "7", which tells the console
to turn on sync-on-green on all the video cards, regardless of how many you
have, or what slot they're in.  This new version requires you to set the value
to correctly match what you have installed.  If you only have 1 video card in
slot 0, then set the variable to "1" and cycle the power.

Been there, done that...

        Stu



