Gaylord Holder (holder@phy.ucsf.edu) wrote:
: I'm trying to set a stripped disk volumn on a 600au running 4.0d and
: advfs and lsm.
: I have 4 Seagate Cheetahs with Ultra interfaces and two Q-logic 1020
: SCSI adapters.

How old is your 600au? All au-series manufactured before March 1, 1998
(serial numbers before ??8100000) do not support extra SCSI controllers
in PCI slots at all due to a problem with PCI bridge. Newer au-series
support ONE additional controller. However, they still not support more
than one (to the total of two controllers including the QLA1040 serving
the internal inclosures).

Try pulling off one of the controllers, and see if that helps. If it does,
you may want to try Qlogic's dual-channel adapter...

Regards,

/Serge.P



