Message-ID: <6ovrta$sqb$1@pegasus.csx.cam.ac.uk>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 373209908
References: <35b2eb51.18596790@10.101.200.105>
Organization: University of Cambridge, England
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

JKChung (onions@doosan.com) wrote:

: Hi,

: I am using OSF/1 4.0b in Alpha 4100 and need to get
: CPU usage % as a return value by program or shell. 
: How do I do this? Thank you. 

If you like ugly C-shell scripts you could do something like this: 

  alias tosec awk -F: "'\\
    {mult=1; for (i=NF;i>0;i--) {sec += "\$"i * mult; mult *= 60} print sec }'"
  set cpu     = `ps -p $pid -otime  | tail -1 | tosec` 
  set elapsed = `ps -p $pid -oetime | tail -1 | tosec` 
  @ percent = ( 100 * $cpu ) / $elapsed

(this is over the lifetime of the process, not current usage a la top).

Mark

