Hello,

I recently answer to Gunter that, for the same problem, I use the
"dxkerneltuner" utility.
When "dxkerneltuner" is started, choose "proc" and then you could modify
the "per-proc-data-size" field. After modification, you must reboot.

PS : I don't reply directly to the news group because I am not sure that
it is the only way to do this modification (and, also, I am not sure of
my english).

