I run 4.05 on 4.0a through 4.0d and it *does* still have numerous problems
foremost of which is exhausting stack and hitting guard pages.  Seems to
be related to gui operations during rendering but no concrete ideas.  One
suggestion is to read the release notes.  There is an environment variable
named something like MOZILLA_USE_ASYNC_DNS which should be set to 'NO' or
'FALSE' as per the notes, the intended effect being to disable async dns.
Once this is done, it still crashes but seems to go into cpu spins less
and you never get the annoying ip lookup message afterwards.

