John Allen wrote:
> 
> Hi:
> 
> I'm running DU 3.2 on an Alphastation 400 4/233.
> 
> I'm wondering why I have a process occupying the majority of the
> cpu resources, with a command of "-sendmail uucp (sendmail)".  It's
> status is 'R'unable and belongs to root.  Can I kill this guy?  Why
> is it happening?

Sendmail = MTA, Mail Transfer Agent. The most popular (and present by default)
	program for handling E-Mail. Comes with SMTP client. Can use any mail
	protocol, if you provide Mail Excanging program. Can handle any type
	of mailbox, if you provide a delivery program.

UUCP = UNIX to UNIX CoPy. An ancient, but in some cases useful, protocol for
	file transfer between two UNIX machines.

Looks like someone configured your machine for UUCP mail transfer. The question
is, do you have UUCP connection and do you use it for mail?

Nix.





