system@tifrvax.tifr.res.in wrote:
> 
> Mail sent when the path to the host/name servers is down bounces back this
> way instead of getting deferred.
> 
> Has anyone else faced this problem and has some solution ?
> 
> I am running Digital Unix 4.0B.

First of all, you should be aware that DEC has it's own templates for
sendmail.cf, which usually makes a "dummy proof" CF file. In return, many things
are not there, even if you install IASS and Sendmail 8.8.7.

Sendmail, usually, bounces back the mail it has no hope of delivering to and it
doesn't care about.

When your network-path is down, sendmail cannot contact the host in question at
all, perhaps DNS fails as well. So, it's hopeless.

When the node is up, but there is no SMTP server on port 25, then there is hope.

> From: Mail Delivery Subsystem <MAILER-DAEMON>
> To: postmast
> Cc: postmaster
> Subject: Returned mail: Host unknown
> 
>    ----- Transcript of session follows -----
> 421 mitvma.mit.edu (smtp)... Deferred: Not owner
> 554 user@mitvma.mit.edu... 550 Host unknown (Authoritative answer from name server): Not owner

DNS doesn't know about mitva.mit.edu and it looks like a hopeless case to
sendmail.

> 
>    ----- Unsent message follows -----
> Received: by tifr.res.in (5.65v3.2/1.1.10.5/30Jun98-0131PM)
>         id AA21389; Wed, 22 Jul 1998 17:44:45 +0530
> Date: Wed, 22 Jul 1998 17:44:45 +0530
> From: General Delivery Postmaster <postmast>
> Message-Id: <9807221214.AA21389@tifr.res.in>
> To: user@mitvma.mit.edu
> Subject: hello
> 
> hello

Nix.





