Okay, I've scanned many newsgroups, read release notes, and added what
I've discovered to produce a shell script for running netscape 4.0x on
du 4.x systems.  It's commented and needs customization for individual
sites.  Try this people and see how it goes:


#!/usr/bin/csh -e
#
# Work is based on knowledge gleaned from many sources and newsgroup postings.
#
# First:  It is recommended that you delete or rename any java_3* files
# in ~/.netscape/.  These have been associated with spins in 4.0x.
#
# I set MOZILLA_HOME in my login scripts.  Subsequent installs and
# updates can then find the native location.
#
#setenv MOZILLA_HOME ~/local/netscape
#
# Augment current library path to pick up old libXt.  To prepare this,
# make a directory 'shlib' in $MOZILLA_HOME.  In this directory, selectively
# make symlinks to files in /usr/lib/netscape which are optionally
# provided by the base system.
#
setenv LD_LIBRARY_PATH $MOZILLA_HOME/shlib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
#
# Add more java classes as needed.
#
#setenv CLASSPATH ~/local/lib/java:$CLASSPATH
#
# I don't set NPX_PLUGIN_PATH as I prefer Netscape's default paths
# for finding plugins.  If you run as root, you should probably
# make the paths explicit.
#
#setenv NPX_PLUGIN_PATH $MOZILLA_HOME/plugins
#
# You can augment nethelp searching with this variable.  It doesn't
# replace the builtin search paths, just adds another directory.
#
#setenv NS_NETHELP_PATH ~/local
#
# Synchronous DNS prevents the address lookup failures.
#
setenv MOZILLA_NO_ASYNC_DNS True
#
# FreeBSD people claim removing the license_accepted token on every
# session prevents the Java-induced CPU-spin hyperactivity.  It also
# forces the user to accept/decline the license agreement on every
# invocation so I disable it.  Note that this doesn't do any file locking.
#
#sed '/browser\.startup\.license_accepted/d' ~/.netscape/preferences.js
>~/.netscape/preferences.js.new
#mv ~/.netscape/preferences.js.new ~/.netscape/preferences.js
#
# If you use CDE and are a software developer or tester, you should
# enable unaligned access fixup printing in your login scripts.  CDE tends
# to disable it.  Then, unless you want to do some debugging on Netscape,
# you'll want to disable this printing (because NS tends to generate
# a lot of unaligned accesses) and set coredumpsize down to 0 so that
# it crashes faster.  When you want to debug a Netscape problem, comment
# these out.
#
uac p 0
limit coredumpsize 0
#
# Try to prevent the 'can't grow stack' crashes unless you want to debug
# them.
#
unlimit stacksize
#
# If you want to see where netscape gets its libraries, enable the
# following variable.
#
#setenv _RLD_ARGS -v
#
# Run it.  Another rumor is that starting java at command time will
# prevent the cpu spins.
#
exec $MOZILLA_HOME/netscape -no-about-splash $*


-- 
