Dave Campbell wrote:
> 
> How I change the login banner on a 4.0B/D D unix box from the standard
> "Digital UNIX (hostname) (terminal)" to prevent the type of system from
> being advertised?

Digital UNIX (formerly DEC OSF/1) supports C2 and can be made to B1 level of
security. I think that one of them (B1, I suspect) states that the machine MUST
identify itself upon login.

Consequently, the message you'd like to avoid should be hard-coded into the
login program.

Nix.




