I am not a big support of using dd to put information onto the tap
drive.  I don't think it is buffered, and getting delays in your network
might cause problems.  The method I would suggest is

	tar cf - <dir name> | gzip -c | rsh <remote host> "gunzip -c >
/dev/st0"

That way you will be sending compressed data over the wire and you
shouldn't have any problems with slow network buffering etc...

Stu.


