------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Interactive Graph Visualization System daVinci V2.1 announced:
------------------------------------------------------------------------

July 13, 1998 (Bremen, Germany)  ---
The University of Bremen and the Bremen Institute of Safe Systems (BISS)
associated with TZI Center for Computing Technology announce:

daVinci V2.1,  the revised edition of the noted visualization system for 
generating high-quality drawings of  directed graphs with more than 3000 
installations worldwide.  Users in the commercial and educational domain 
have already  integrated daVinci as user interface  of their application 
programs for  visualizing hierarchies,  dependency structures, networks,  
configuration diagrams,  dataflows, and so on.  daVinci combines hierar-
chical  graph layout with powerful  interactive capabilities  and an API 
for remote access from a connected application.

Features at a glance:

  * Automatic graph layout with edge crossing- and bend minimization.
  * Incremental graph layout
  * Interactive fine tuning for a given layout.
  * Many attributes for nodes and edges (color, font, shapes, ...).
  * Visualization definitions.
  * Interactive abstractions (collapsing subgraphs, hiding edges).
  * Scaling operations for getting an overview.
  * Encapsulated PostScript output.
  * API for communication with an underlying application program.
  * Interactive graph editor as demo application.
  
What's new in daVinci V2.1:

  * Fully incremental graph layout
  * Subgraph abstractions using incremental layout
  * Completely rewritten, much faster graph layout algorithm
  * New automatic layout functions
  * Fine-Tuning for all layout orientations
  * Visualization rules (API)
  * Pop-Up menus for nodes and edges (API)
  * Drag and Drop for nodes and edges (API)
  * All open windows accessible via API commands
  * Some more enhancements to the API
  * New command-line options
  * New Attributes for Nodes and Edges
  * Graph editor supports all new API features, including drag and drop
  * Graph editor can now load status files
  * Reduced memory footprint
  * Strongly improved reliability due to automated testing 
  
Voices of daVinci V2.1 beta testers:

  "We  have just replaced the old daVinci version by the new one for our
   application  KIV and  everything worked much  better than before. The
   incremental graph-layout  is an  impressive new  feature and  the new
   layout algorithm works much better than the old one."
  Kurt Stenzel, University of Ulm
  
The daVinci project would like  to acknowledge the  efforts of all  beta
testers  who helped  to improve the quality  of daVinci V2.1, especially
Gero Streng from University of Stuttgart.

More information about daVinci is available in WWW:
  
    http://www.tzi.de/~davinci/
  
daVinci V2.1 is licensed free of charge  for non-profit use and is imme-
diately available for the following UNIX operating systems:  Sun Solaris 
2.x, SunOS 4.x, Linux (ELF S.u.S.e., RedHat4, RedHat5), IBM AIX 4.2, SGI
Irix. HPUX will follow shortly. The daVinci  system can be downloaded by
anonymous ftp from:

    ftp://ftp.tzi.DE/tzi/biss/daVinci/

In this directory, there are tar-archives (compressed with gzip) for all
supported OS platforms.  The content is the same  for all distributions,  
except of the binaries. The sources are not available. Each distribution 
covers daVinci,  the HTML online documentation,  examples and tools.  To 
contact the daVinci project, to send bugs, to suggest new features or to  
subscribe to the mailing list, please write by e-mail to: 

    daVinci@tzi.DE

