Craig Paul wrote:
> 
> Has anybody gotten QPOPPER 2.52 to work with D Unix 4.0D with enhanced
> security? If so, what did you have to change in the makefile?

I've just done it today. Well, here's the story...

1. If you run C2SEC on your Digital UNIX, you must add -DAUTH to your Makefile.
But, that CRASHED my compilation, because there is a structure in
/usr/include/rpc/auth.h with the same name!

2. So, I changed pop_pass.c, replaced AUTH keyword with C2SEC keyword. Of
course, the Makefile had to be changed too, with -DC2SEC, instead of -DAUTH.

3. The compilation went fine. And then I found out the hard way, that there is
another "#ifdef AUTH" statement, this time, in popper.h file. Changed that too
and it worked OK. The message on POP3 server for this error was like this:
"Authentication database not initialised".

My E-Mail at work is <nikola@ev.ns.ac.yu> If you need additional help, my
Makefile, just howl.

Nix.




