> cc: Severe: includes.h, line 125: Cannot find file <stdio.h> specified in
> #include directive.
> 
> I checked inside the includes.h file, and line 125 is commented out like so:
> #include <stdio.h>

Actually, that's not "commented out". It's actually a preprocessor
directive that says to include the contents of the file "stdio.h"
here. This translates to the file /usr/include/stdio.h.

My guess is that you do not have this file installed on your V4.0D
system. You will need to install the OSFINCLUDE425 subset to get
the "Standard Header Files (Software Development)".

Here's what I see on my V4.0D system:

% /usr/sbin/setld -i | grep OSFINCLUDE
OSFINCLUDE425        installed  Standard Header Files (Software Development)

Note that it should say "installed", if you try this on your system.

-Jeff

