The best way to find out what has changed is to look at the relevant
parts of the "Release Notes" documents.  These are available on
the Web at
	http://www.UNIX.digital.com/faqs/publications/pub_page/doc_list.html

Unfortunately, to find out what has changed between 3.2G and V4.0D,
you might have to read the release notes for V4.0, V4.0A, V4.0B, and
V4.0D (I'm not sure whether all of these versions have AdvFS changes).

The release notes describe new features, and known bugs in the
version documented, but I'm not sure that they specifically
document bugs that have been fixed since the previous version.
I've been told, by both the AdvFS developers and people who use
AdvFS, that they have made many improvements in the performance
and reliability of the file system.  However, I don't have any
personal experience managing an AdvFS system.

-Jeff



