Steve Briggs wrote:
> 
> Just noticed a strange file /etc/.AM_is_running. I renamed it and
> surprise dxaccounts started running again. I had another server with the
> same problem. What causes it ? anything to do with C2 ?

AM_is_running == AccountManager_is_running ; Account Manager ==
dxaccounts

It's a dxaccounts lock file, preventing multiple users from accessing
and modifying user databases. I don't think that this detail is specific
to C2 sec, because you can start dxaccounts on BASE sec level.

Personally, I always install C2. After surviving couple of irritating
situations, I can handle it and I like it.

Nix.




