We just bought seven Digital Personal Workstationm 500au, our first
DEC machines.  We want to run Digital UNIX 4.0D on those boxes.
Digital's Installation Guide is painfully incomplete in guiding
the administrator through the installation process.
For example, there is no advice on whether to pick AdvFS or
UFS filessytems, and whether to enable LSM.  The worst, though,
is the missing description of installing those blasted licenses,
a real Digital Special !

Well, after numerous calls to Digital experts we finally made it,
and I wrote a guide "Installing Digital UNIX 4.0" available
to everyone on this Web page:

   http://www.fysik.dtu.dk/digital_unix.html

This guide is supposed to tell you everything that Digital
forgot to tell you, actually supplementing the Installation
Guide and the CD-ROM installation utilities.  This has become
my personal guide for future installations.

I hope that my guide will become useful to others as well,
and I would welcome feedback for improving the guide.  Maybe
one day Digital will even write a guide that covers these
topics ?:-)

