> The syslogd shipped with the original 4.0D is broken
> (or the documentation is broken, it depends on your point of
> view) and does not allow any remote logging. In order to enable
> remote logging with plain 4.0D, you'll have to create an
> (undocumented) file /etc/syslog.auth. Since its not documented (<g>),
