Thanks for an interesting tip. I sometimes like to get syslog messages
from an Ascend Pipeline 50 router when I am debugging ISDN connection
problems. It works fine logging to a 4.0a machine, but it has never
worked logging to a 4.0d machine. I thought it might be something
related to having two ethernet cards, but it looks like that wasn't the
problem.

By the way, you have to put the canonical host name in syslog.auth
(presumably whatever gethostbyaddr returns). It doesn't seem to work
with just an IP address.
