Roy Smith wrote:
> 
> Is there any way to get the kernel to log more information about file
> system full events?  The process id that caused it, or the pathname of the
> file, or anything which might give us a clue what's going on?

One possibility: turn on audit for suspected (or for all) users and select all
system calls that have anything to do with writing or creating files. Audit logs
got to /var/audit/, so it will log.

Then use either audit_tool or dxaudit to extract just failures of those system
calls.

It is a little painful, but it'll get you there.

Nix.




